Z||000000||bcibob670||07-24-2000||06:56 AM||||86 2.5 L  autotrans.  after replacing every sensor , ecm ,every ignition part (incuding new distributor) <BR>I HAVE DISCOVERED THAT THE ELECTRICAL HARNESS HAS A PROBLEM ONCE THE ENGINE HEATS IT UP AND I HIT A FEW BUMPS THE PROBLEM IS SOMEWHERE BETWEEN THE DISTRIBUTOR AND THE BATTERY WALL JUNCTION.  <P>THE PROBLEM SHUTS OFF THE FUEL .  BY PULLING ON THE HARNESS FROM THE BATTERY SIDE IT SOLVES THE PROBLEM.   of course im gonna replace the harness , it would be tough to drive and hold on to it.   hee hee hee...<BR>I would have to give my self a ticket   LOL.||||reg||4
Z||000001||StuGood||07-24-2000||02:40 PM||||Way to go-!  Knew a crime scene investigator could track down the culprit  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> !<P>By the way, know where I can buy an ECM and distributor for cheap?  Just kidding  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  Always good to have spares around for next time.<P>Might want to check any connector terminals carefully, before you replace the entire harness.  In any case, glad you found the problem.<P>    ||||reg||10
Z||000002||84 Indy||07-24-2000||06:28 PM||||Before you replace the harness check the fusible link by the starter if this is bad it will cause the same symtoms you described. Replace it even if it's only slightly frayed.  Besides there cheap.||||reg||1
